Hi Anthropic team,

I’m an independent developer building an open-source autonomous AI agent system inspired by JARVIS-like architectures.

My project focuses on multi-model orchestration, combining different AI systems (LLMs, tools, APIs) into a unified agent capable of real-world task execution. The goal is to move beyond simple chatbots and build production-ready AI systems that can act, automate, and scale.

While the project is still growing and may not yet have large star counts, it addresses a critical gap in the ecosystem: integrating multiple AI models into a single modular system for practical use.

I actively develop:
- Agent-based architectures
- Multi-model routing systems
- Automation workflows

Access to Claude Max would significantly enhance development, especially for long-context reasoning, multi-agent workflows, and system-level experimentation.

Thank you for supporting open-source developers.

